  "body": "## What changed\n\nPR #2731 made the STEP chord report true: the report is the highest kept facet edge times the inside bound of the face kind (#2718). `step_fit::fit` never splits a boundary edge. The kernel held the boundary edges only to the pass tolerance. Thus each model with a cone, sphere or torus face read 1.5 x the tolerance and became reduced fidelity. On `fig8.step`, three `shoulder_adaptive` tests failed (main is red, #2754).\n\nThis PR divides each shell edge before the pass by the largest inside bound of its faces:\n\n- `step_fit::edge_divisors`: 1.5 for an edge of a cone, sphere or torus face, 1 for all other edges. A cylinder face then gives the largest divisor of its edges to all of its edges, until no edge changes. A wall meshes rim to rim. Two rims with different points make slanted wall facets, and each slice height then cuts a different chord of the wall.\n- `CurveGuard::finer` (`step_division.rs`): the edge polyline divides the pass tolerance by that divisor.\n- `step_guard::Guarded::new` sets the divisor for each edge.\n\nThe edge is divided one time, in the shell's own polyline. Both faces of the edge get the same points, so the shell stays closed. The 1.5 bound and the #2731 report do not change. No test expectation changes.\n\n## Readings (fig8.step)\n\n| Reading | Before (main) | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| reported chord (`coarse_mm`) | 0.00749264 mm (reduced fidelity) | 0.005 mm (full fidelity) |\n| facets | 7822 | 7974 |\n| outer outline loop (`slice::project`, 64) | 2520 points | 3314 points |\n| `shoulder_adaptive` | 3 failed | 8 passed, 1 ignored |\n\nA trial divisor of 2.0 (1.5 with a margin of 4/3) also gave 0.005 mm. But the fig8 Adaptive2D path then ended with an extra ring at the stock edge after the wall pass. The minimum distance to the part stayed 4.000 mm, so there was no gouge. I dropped that divisor. The exact bound (1.5) keeps the path order. The sensitivity of the path order is filed as #2759.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `step_fidelity::a_model_with_faces_curved_two_ways_reports_full_fidelity` (new; fails on main with 0.00749).\n- `geometry::import::step_fit::tests::edge_divisors_hold_two_way_faces_and_match_cylinder_rims` (new unit test).\n- `shoulder_adaptive`: `fig8_bottom_face_outside_containment_generates_and_stops_at_face`, `fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works`, `outside_containment_air_band_fixture_blocks_post` (green again, expectations not changed).\n\nRun one by one: `shoulder_adaptive`, `step_fidelity`, `step_chord_units`, `step_budget`, `tilted_gouge`, the `geometry::import::step` lib tests. Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 22 steps, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --lib --tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `tilted_gouge_kinds`: there is no such test target in `camcraft-app`.\n- The kernel `step_agreement` and `feature_edge_g1_join` suites (known red on main, #2713): not run, not changed.\n- Models with sphere or torus faces from outside the fixtures. Where an edge curve's parameter midpoint and the face's differ, the report can go over the tolerance. It then says reduced fidelity; it is never under-stated.\n- No golden toolpath or G-code file changed. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Note\n\nPR #2728 (fork, `needs-rework`, #2713) also changes `step_fit.rs`. This PR does not touch its concern (the flip of a flat cap facet) or `crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement.rs`.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/2754-step-boundary-split.md`.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: STEP import: models with cone, sphere or torus faces are full fidelity again; their boundary edges are divided finer so that the reported chord meets the 0.005 mm cap.\n\nFixes #2754\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
